  "cli_result_text": "## Summary of the root cause\n\n**Babel side** (`packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts`): the plugin branches on `options.legacy` / `options.version === \"legacy\"`. When legacy, it uses `transformer-legacy.ts`, whose visitor builds `applyDecoratedDescriptor`/`initializerWarningHelper` calls \u2014 this is the pre-TC39, TypeScript-compatible decorator form NestJS depends on. `@babel/plugin-transform-typescript` (`packages/babel-plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts`) itself doesn't touch decorators at all (it only strips types/enums/namespaces and leaves `node.decorators` untouched on class members), so plugin **order** in the Babel config only matters insofar as `plugin-proposal-decorators` must run before `plugin-transform-typescript` strips other TS-only syntax that decorators may depend on (parameter properties, type annotations feeding into `Reflect.metadata`) \u2014 Babel's legacy decorator transform doesn't itself emit `Reflect.metadata` calls; that requires a separate plugin (e.g. `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata`) reading the TS type annotations before `plugin-transform-typescript` strips them.\n\n**SWC side**: `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs` wires `TransformConfig.legacy_decorator` \u2192 `decorators::Config.legacy` and `TransformConfig.decorator_metadata` \u2192 `decorators::Config.emit_metadata`, both passed into `swc_ecma_transforms_proposal::decorators::decorators()` (`decorators/mod.rs`). That function dispatches to `decorators::legacy::new(emit_metadata)` (`decorators/legacy/mod.rs`) only when `legacy: true`; the non-legacy code path explicitly does `unimplemented!(\"emitting decorator metadata while using new proposal\")` if `emit_metadata` is set. Inside the legacy path, `TscDecorator::visit_mut_class` only invokes `Metadata::new(...)` (`decorators/legacy/metadata.rs`, which emits `design:type`/`design:paramtypes`/`design:returntype` via `_ts_metadata`/`Reflect.metadata`) **when `self.metadata` is true** \u2014 i.e., only when `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata: true` is set in `.swcrc`, in addition to `legacyDecorator: true`.\n\n**The divergence**: Babel's legacy decorator transform \"just works\" for DI because the ecosystem convention pairs it with a metadata-emitting plugin/preset (or `@babel/preset-typescript` + reflect-metadata tooling) that customers often get for free via NestJS's documented Babel setup. SWC requires **two independent, non-implied flags** (`jsc.transform.legacyDecorator: true` AND `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata: true`) \u2014 `legacyDecorator` alone reproduces the decorator *call* shape but silently produces zero `Reflect.metadata`/`design:*` calls, since `TscDecorator.metadata` defaults false and the modern-decorator path can't emit metadata at all. A customer who only set `legacyDecorator: true` (matching Babel's `legacy: true`) without also setting `decoratorMetadata: true` gets classes that construct fine (`@injectable()` still runs as a decorator) but no `Reflect.getMetadata` design-type data \u2014 exactly the \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading getMetadata)\" NestJS IoC failure, because Nest's `ModuleRef`/`Injector` resolves constructor param types via `Reflect.getMetadata(\"design:paramtypes\", ...)`, which was never written.",
